--> Casual is the one unranked competition type (DEC-233). Rows a dev or
--> restore seed wrote as practice become casual before the CHECK tightens.
UPDATE "rooms" SET "competition_type" = 'casual' WHERE "competition_type" = 'practice';--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "rounds" SET "competition_type" = 'casual' WHERE "competition_type" = 'practice';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "rooms" DROP CONSTRAINT "rooms_competition_type_check", ADD CONSTRAINT "rooms_competition_type_check" CHECK ("competition_type" in ('ranked', 'casual'));--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "rounds" DROP CONSTRAINT "rounds_competition_type_check", ADD CONSTRAINT "rounds_competition_type_check" CHECK ("competition_type" in ('ranked', 'casual'));--> statement-breakpoint
--> One-on-one revision 2: the 1AR defaults to 3:00 (DEC-234). Revision 1
--> stays, so every Room, Round and preset pinned to it keeps its rules
--> (ADR 0058). The rows mirror packages/db/src/reference-formats.ts; the
--> sync test fails when they drift.
